  "steps": [
    "Crush ⅓ cup (40g or 3 pieces) digestive biscuits into a fine powder, Add 20g melted butter and mix well, Press the mixture firmly into the bottom of your tub to create an even base.",
    "Add to a blender ⅔ cup (150g) low-fat paneer, ¾ cup (170g) cream cheese, 3 tbsp (60g) honey, ½ tsp (1g) coffee powder, 2 tbsp (30ml) skim milk, 1 tsp vanilla extract, ½ cup (100g) melted dark chocolate, A pinch of salt, Blend until completely smooth and creamy.",
    "(I used 60ml of milk, but it made the filling a little runny, so I’d recommend sticking to 30ml.)",
    "Pour the cheesecake filling over the biscuit base and spread it evenly, Let it set in the fridge for at least 1 hour.",
    "½ cup (50g) dark chocolate, ¼ cup (50g) heavy cream, 1 tbsp (15g) butter.",
    "Pour the ganache over the cheesecake and let it set.",
    "Or, keep it lighter and simply dust some cocoa powder over the top like I did.",
    "And your Healthy Cheesecake Tub is ready!"
  ],
